Venezuela's main Consulate in Colombia's  capital Bogota lies in Ruins an  accidental fire in April burned much of  it its walls covered in graffiti and  overgrown weeds it's a tangible symbol  of a relationship gone sour since 2019  when Colombia's former president Ivan  Duke refused to recognize Nicolas Maduro  as the president of Venezuela after  elections Duca said were fraudulent  but all that has changed with the  election of Colombia's first leftist  president Gustavo Pedro who promised to  restore relations  last month Maduro enthusiastically  received Colombia's newly appointed  Ambassador emitting big on laughs and  hugs the Colombian invoice says the  neighbors should never have parted ways  there are some 5 million Colombian  citizens that have been totally  abandoned for years without possibility  to renew a passport and ID it was just  stupid and inhumane whatever the  difference is it doesn't make sense to  have no Communications  the two countries have since announced a  full reopening of their porous 2000  kilometers long border for trade  called for the resumption of military  collaboration in a region overrun by  criminal groups  but despite the many pledges and  boastful announcements restoring full  diplomatic relations is easier said than  done cut the two countries remain deeply  suspicious of one another  I think it will be a much more complex  and long process than what people think  the two countries have deeper symmetries  if you look at trade Venezuela's  industry is in shambles for the Maduro  regime the most important thing is to  show that they're not as isolated as  they were while Colombia had a lot to  gain economically but wants to avoid  being seen as cozing up to a less than  democratic government yeah rival of  Venezuelan Ambassador in Colombia was a  noticeable muted Affair and the  countries have so far avoided addressing  Venezuela's ongoing political crisis and  the fate of the more than 2.5 million  refugees in Colombia the agenda makes no  mention of security of migration of  consulate Services Venezuela's  Ambassador Placencia has long denied the  existence of a migratory crisis but now  that he's in Bogota he inevitably will  have to recognize it and address it but  even with its many fits and starts the  fact that the two neighbors are talking  again is welcome news for millions of  Colombians and Venezuelans on both sides  of the Border they've been in limbo for  years but now believe there's hope for a  more stable future Alessandra Al Jazeera  Bogota
 

